# Project 1 - Raspberry Pi Setup

## Objective

Learn the Raspberry Pi ecosystem and prepare it for future engineering projects. While I had done labs briefly like this in College, I always wanted to circle back and relearn this on my own time. 

## Hardware

- Raspberry Pi 5 (8 GB)
- CanaKit Starter Kit
- Wired keyboard and mouse
- Monitor
- Bread board and electronics starter kit

## Software

- Raspberry Pi OS
- Python 3 / Thonny

## Goals

- Boot Raspberry Pi
- Connect to Wi-Fi
- Enable SSH
- Learn Linux basics
- Run first Python program
- Relearn breadboard basics

## Status

Completed.

## Challenges

No challenges faced in assembling and powering on Raspberry Pi. Basic program was ran to test "Hello world!".

Follow up challenge to connect Raspberry Pi to Breadboard and blink an LED in 1 second intervals.
Research was needed to figure out some coding terminalogy. 
Breadboard wiring was accomplished through trial and error. 


